
~(mirror-mung)

(mirror-room-desc)
    You are in a large square room with tall ceilings.  On the south wall
    is an enormous mirror which fills the entire wall.  There are exits
    on the other three sides of the room.
    (if) (mirror-mung) (then)
        Unfortunately, you have managed to destroy it by your reckless
        actions.
    (endif)

%% MIRR1
#mirror-room1
(room *)
(name *)	Mirror Room
(inherently dark *)
(look *)
    (mirror-room-desc)
(from * go #west to #cold-passage)
(from * go #north to #steep-crawlway)
(from * go #east to #cave1)
(* attracts #mirror)

%% MIRR2
#mirror-room2
(room *)
(name *)	Mirror Room
(look *)
    (mirror-room-desc)
(from * go #west to #winding-passage)
(from * go #north to #narrow-crawlway)
(from * go #east to #cave2)
(* attracts #mirror)

#mirror
(name *)	mirror
(descr *)
    ~(mirror-mung)There is an ugly person staring at you.
(descr *)
    (mirror-mung)The mirror is broken into many pieces.

%% TODO: object action routine MIRROR-MIRROR

(perform [feel #mirror])
    ~(mirror-mung)
    There is a rumble from deep within the earth and the room shakes.
    (if) (current room #mirror-room1) (then)
        (now)(#player is #in #mirror-room2)
    (else)
        (now)(#player is #in #mirror-room1)
    (endif)

(perform [feel #mirror])
    (mirror-mung)
    Nobody but a greedy surgeon would allow you to attempt that trick.

(perform [attack #mirror])
    ~(mirror-mung)
    (now)(mirror-mung)
    You have broken the mirror.  I hope you have a seven years supply of
    good luck handy.

(perform [attack #mirror])
    (mirror-mung)Haven't you done enough already?
